# seat-ux — round 7 working notes (append-only)

## Session log

### Frame pass (static reads, before driving)

Fixture clock verified consistent across all three products: Timeline states
"TODAY IS 16 JULY" / "Today, 16 July"; Notes group head says "Thursday 16 July,
today"; Tasks shows 14 Jul as the single overdue chip and "Today" on the run-sheet.
Measure arithmetic on the across axis checks out to the pixel: today x=209,
wedding x=1876, 79 days -> 21.1px/day; every tick (16/23/37/44/51/65) lands within
1.5px of daysFromToday x px-per-day. Weekday names are right for 2026.
Header counts check out: board 5 of 13 = 38%, lanes 3+3+2+0+5 = 13, "5 with no day"
matches the 5 dateless cards. Dense 9 of 32 = 28%, lanes 10+7+4+2+9 = 32, and each
"N more below" reconciles with the lane count.

CANDIDATES (to be verified by driving):
1. notes head names one notebook ("Mara & Finn  Saturday 3 October, in 79 days")
   verbatim identical to the first index group head, ~484px below it; and it does
   NOT change when the desk is holding a note filed under "The house" (seam state)
   or when the review queue spans every notebook (review state).
2. across measure: labels above the line read (outward) number > date > title;
   labels below the line read number > title > date. The mirror is not a mirror.
3. tasks head carries the completion fact three ways: "5 of 13 done" + bar + "38%".
   The phone drops the 38%, which suggests it is the non-load-bearing one.
4. dictation floor disclosure sentence 2 is about *typing*, on a surface where you
   are speaking. Also "LISTENING 0:00" over a finished transcript.
5. floating capsule overlaps list rows at 768 - check whether the scroller reserves
   its band at the true bottom.

### FINDING 1 (confirmed by measurement) — notes-head-scope-is-invisible

`.headNext` in the Notes head — "Mara & Finn / Saturday 3 October, in 79 days" —
is a real, working scope filter: `<button data-act="scope" aria-pressed="false"
aria-label="...Press to see only these notes.">`, and pressing it narrows the
index from 14 rows to 3, flips the h1 to "Your notes, narrowed", underlines
itself and prints an "All 14 notes" way-out pill. All of that is good work.

The problem is that NOTHING on screen says it is pressable until after you have
pressed it.

Measured at 1920, notes.notebook, rest vs :hover on `.headNext`, every computed
property of the button and both of its children:

  REST   bg rgba(0,0,0,0) | shadow none | border 0px | text-decoration none |
         b color rgb(17,17,17) | span color rgba(17,17,17,.72) | cursor pointer
  HOVER  identical. CHANGED KEYS: []  (zero properties differ)

And the rendered crop of the head band (700x60 at 900,55) is BYTE-IDENTICAL
between rest and hover: 1300 bytes, `Buffer.equals` true.

Cause is one line, `_gate-suite.html:4441`:
  [data-app="notes"] .headNext:hover b { color: var(--ink); }
with `--ink-1: var(--ink)` at :4194. The hover rule repaints #111111 as #111111.

At rest the control also carries no chevron, no rule, no fill, no underline. Its
sibling in Tasks — the identical job, switching what you are looking at — is
`.projSwitch`, which ships an SVG chevron. So the suite has two project/scope
switchers in the same head slot and only one of them looks like a control.

Consequence for Orla: the head reads as a single sentence — "All your notes,
Mara & Finn, Saturday 3 October, in 79 days" — which is a false statement of what
is on screen (14 notes across four notebooks). The one control that would make it
true is invisible, and the affordance only arrives after the state has changed.

### FINDING 2 (confirmed by measurement) — across-measure-label-order-flips

timeline.owner-flight @1920, across axis. Rail `.b-rail` at y=682. Distance of each
label's optical centre from the rail, measured in the DOM:

  ABOVE the rail, outward:  b-away "16"  35px  ->  b-date "Sat 1 Aug"  51px
                            ->  b-title "Menu tasting..."  73-85px
  BELOW the rail, outward:  b-away "23"  35px  ->  b-title "Send the invitations" 56px
                            ->  b-date "Sat 8 Aug"  78px

The day-count is symmetric to the pixel (35/35). The title and the date SWAP rings
across the rail. Holds for all seven moments: 16/37/51/79 above read number-date-title,
23/44/65 below read number-title-date.

Cause, `_gate-suite.html:8544-8556`: `.b-copy` (children in DOM order title, date) is
mirrored as a BLOCK by swapping `bottom:` for `top:`, but its internal order is never
reversed. So above the rail the last child (date) ends up nearest and the first child
(title) farthest.

Consequences: the titles - the only thing on the measure that says what a moment IS -
do not form a band; they alternate 73px above / 56px below, on opposite sides of their
own dates. And the below-line order (number, title, date) is the order the down layout
and the phone use, so the four above-line moments are the only place in the product
that reads number-date-title.

Not a locked-architecture question and not a colour: one declaration.

### Checked and CLEAN (not findings — recording so the panel knows they were driven)
- Every count on every surface reconciles through one accessor: notes index
  8 to decide / 14 notes vs five group tails (1+1+3+2+1=8, 3+1+5+3+1=14); tasks
  5 of 13 / 38% / lane counts / "5 with no day"; dense 9 of 32 / 28% / three
  "N more below" rows; after the seam crossing 5 of 14 / 36% / "6 with no day" /
  To do 4 / notes 8->7 to decide and 3->4 already in Tasks. Nothing drifts.
- Tab order at 1920 on tasks.board is 18 stops with a real roving model (one rail
  tile, one card, one seg item, one tray Add). No dead stops, no body traps.
- `.cardDots` is opacity 0 at rest but 1 on :hover, :focus AND under
  `@media (pointer: coarse)`. Not an invisible-focusable defect.
- Planning open @1440 does NOT delete Done: the sheet becomes a real scroller
  (948/916) and `.sheet::after` is a MEASURED 96px fade toggled by
  `data-more-right`/`data-more-left` — opacity 0 when nothing is hidden, 1 when
  something is, and it swaps ends when you scroll. That whole lessons class is closed.
- The overdue filter states itself ("Showing 1 overdue task. 12 others are
  hidden." + "Show all work"), badges Show, and converts every lane count to
  "shown/total" (0/3, 1/3, 0/2, 0, 0/5). Header honesty under filter is done.
- The seam crossing announces once ("Sent to Tasks. Your note stayed here. In
  The house." then "Opened in Tasks. Your note stayed in Notes."), leaves focus
  on a surviving control, lands the card in To do and offers 30s undo.
- Timeline behind-you is a native <details>/<summary>; folded and open notes are
  both true against the three rows.

### FINDING 3 (HEADLINE, confirmed by measurement) — list-tick-never-shows-done

In List view — which is the ONLY view a phone gets, and the only view below the
board's 1199 floor — a completed task's checkbox is drawn identically to an
uncompleted one. Not similar. Identical.

Measured: for a `.lrow[data-done]` and a `.lrow` without it, I diffed 33 computed
properties across the element and both pseudo-elements (backgroundColor, boxShadow,
borderColor/Width, color, opacity, content, width, height, transform,
backgroundImage) plus the SVG's color/opacity/stroke and the check path's
stroke/opacity/stroke-width:

  LIST @390   changed properties: 0
  LIST @768   changed properties: 0
  LIST @1440 (chosen from the Board/List switch, not a fallback): 0
  BOARD @1920 changed properties: 11 (bg -> rgb(17,17,17), ring removed,
              colour/stroke -> white, check path painted)

Driven, not just read. On a 390 phone I tapped the tick on "Confirm marquee sides
with the hire company":

  BEFORE  bg rgba(0,0,0,0) | box-shadow inset 0 0 0 1.4px rgba(17,17,17,.28)
          | color rgba(0,0,0,0) | aria-checked=false | name "Mark done"
  AFTER   bg rgba(0,0,0,0) | box-shadow inset 0 0 0 1.4px rgba(17,17,17,.28)
          | color rgba(0,0,0,0) | aria-checked=true  | name "Mark not done"

The control she pressed did not change one pixel. The feedback is elsewhere: a lane
word 300px to the right flips "TO DO" -> "DONE", the pip goes green, a "16 Jul" chip
appears at the far right, and the title drops from #111 to rgba(17,17,17,.62).
Screenshots `_zz-ph-tick-before/after.png` show the ring empty in both.

Root cause, single and precise: every done-state rule for `.tick` is scoped to the
BOARD card, and the list row is `.lrow`, not `.card` —
  2326  .card[data-done] .tick { background: var(--ink); box-shadow:none; color:var(--white) }
  2535-6 .card[data-just-done] .tick { animation: tickSettle } / svg path { checkDraw }
  3160-1 .card[data-done] .tick:hover/:focus-visible { box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--wash-2) }
  3193-4 (forced-colors) .card:not([data-done]) .tick svg { display:none } /
         .card[data-done] .tick { background: CanvasText; color: Canvas }
`listRow()` at 12686 emits `<article class="lrow" ... data-done>` with
`<button class="tick" role="checkbox" aria-checked="true" aria-label="Mark not done">`.
So the accessibility tree is correct and the render contradicts it.

The forced-colors pair inverts the same bug: because `.card:not([data-done])` never
matches a list row, in Windows High Contrast every list tick paints its check —
verified with forcedColors:"active" at 390, svgDisplay "block" on all 13 rows,
8 of which are not done. On the board the same emulation correctly gives "none"
for not-done and "block" for done.

FIX (one edit, no new colour, no new weight, nothing architectural): widen those
five selector groups from `.card[data-done]` / `.card[data-just-done]` /
`.card:not([data-done])` to `:is(.card, .lrow)[data-done]` etc. The treatment
already exists and is already ratified on the board; it is simply not reaching
the list.

Why this is the headline: the tick is the most-pressed control in the product; the
list is the phone's only view; and a venue manager standing in a marquee ticking
jobs off gets no confirmation from the thing under her thumb. It is also the one
place on this whole surface where the pixels and the accessible name say opposite
things.
